\u0026 Utilities","description":"Power \u0026 Utilities","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#babylon-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"babylon-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-19T15:11:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-14T23:32:28+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"Founded in 2013, Babylon is a subscription health service provider that enables users to have virtual consultations with doctors and health care professionals via text and video messaging through its mobile application. Using AWS, the company can innovate using artificial intelligence and scale globally.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Babylon_Customer-Reference_Logo.809c8654f7ba94c681cf545c94bda551127e919c.png","displayLocation":"United Kingdom","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eFounded in 2013, Babylon (Babylonhealth.com) is a subscription health service provider that enables users to have virtual consultations with doctors and health care professionals via text and video messaging through its mobile application. Watch Dr. Ali Parsa, CEO and founder at Babylon, discuss how AWS allows the company to innovate with artificial intelligence and scale globally.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Healthcare","sortDate":"2018-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/babylon/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Babylon","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2018","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Babylon Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#video","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Video","des