"description":"Case Study","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Serverless","description":"Serverless","dateCreated":"2021-07-28T18:46:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#nigeria","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Nigeria","description":"Nigeria","dateCreated":"2020-04-09T03:55:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Storage","description":"Storage","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#software-internet","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Software \u0026 Internet","description":"Software \u0026 Internet","dateCreated":"2020-06-25T04:08:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#ssa","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Sub-Saharan Africa","description":"Sub-Saharan Africa","dateCreated":"2020-03-10T05:18:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#customer-segment#smb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#customer-segment","name":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","description":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:15+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#epic-games-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"epic-games-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-19T15:15:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-19T03:04:48+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"Epic Games uses AWS to deliver Fortnite to more than 200 million players around the world, support growth of more than 100 times in just 12 months, and perform analysis that helps it improve the game. Fortnite, one of the world\u0027s most popular video games, runs nearly entirely on AWS, including its worldwide game-server fleet, backend services, databases, websites, and analytics pipeline and processing systems.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/EpicGames_Customer-Reference_Logo.8a439eccad8e4f56fc6f9733371dfecc459b5ba3.png","displayLocation":"Americas","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eChris Dyl, director of platform at EPIC Games, discusses how AWS is powering its creation engine Unreal Engine and the last-man-standing game Fortnite. As the engine behind one of the world\u0019s most popular games with millions of concurrent players worldwide, EPIC relies on AWS to help it reach the scale and the elasticity it needs to provide the best player experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Gaming","sortDate":"2018-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/EPICGames/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Epic Games","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2018","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Epic Games Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Kinesis","description":"Amazon Kinesis","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:04:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:45+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","description":"Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#customer-story","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Customer Story","description":"Customer Story","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#gaming","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Gaming","description":"Gaming","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:04+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Serverless","description":"Serverless","dateCreated":"2021-07-28T18:46:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#emr","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon EMR","description":"Amazon EMR","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:03:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:36+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Storage","description":"Storage","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#americas","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Americas","description":"Americas","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:29+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#video","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Video","description":"Video","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:11+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Analytics","description":"Analytics","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:22+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#innovator","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Innovator","description":"Innovator","dateCreated":"2022-04-05T21:17:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-06-27T20:43:35+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#innovator#epic-games","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#innovator","name":"Epic Games","description":"Epic Games","dateCreated":"2022-04-25T19:06:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-07-16T00:04:47+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#amazon-items-and-offers-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"amazon-items-and-offers-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-19T15:11:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-19T03:04:55+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"Amazon migrated its Item Master Service from Oracle to Amazon DynamoDB to improve availability and scalability, reduce operational burden, and improve utilization. Amazon used AWS Database Migration Service to migrate 150 TB of data in just two months with zero downtime, and now relies on Amazon DynamoDB to process more than five billion catalog updates every day without significant manual effort.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/amazon-logo-1x.a64c3eedfb84347ecf50e210637c0cf810922e10.png","displayLocation":"Americas","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon migrated its Item Master Service from Oracle to Amazon DynamoDB to improve availability and scalability, reduce operational burden, and improve utilization. Amazon used AWS Database Migration Service to migrate 150 TB of data in just two months with zero downtime, and now relies on Amazon DynamoDB to process more than five billion catalog updates every day without significant manual effort.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Retail","sortDate":"2018-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/itemsandoffers/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Amazon","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2018","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Amazon Items and Offers Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"customer-references#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise","description":"Enterprise","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:39:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-05T01:27:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#dynamodb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon DynamoDB","description":"Amazon DynamoDB","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:31+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Serverless","description":"Serverless","dateCreated":"2021-07-28T18:46:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#americas","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Americas","description":"Americas","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:29+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Migration","description":"Migration","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:28+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Databases","description":"Databases","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-12T02:01:30+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#use-case#general-database-migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#use-case","name":"General Database Migration","description":"General Database Migration","dateCreated":"2020-06-05T06:37:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:41+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#database-migration-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Database Migration Service (DMS)","description":"AWS Database Migration Service (DMS)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:27+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#customer-story","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Customer Story","description":"Customer Story","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#retail","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Retail","description":"Retail","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Databases","description":"Databases","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:27+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#case-study","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Case Study","description":"Case Study","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#database-migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Database Migration","description":"Database Migration","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-12T02:01:30+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise (ENT)","description":"Enterprise (ENT)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#innovator","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Innovator","description":"Innovator","dateCreated":"2022-04-05T21:17:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-06-27T20:43:35+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#innovator#amazon","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#innovator","name":"Amazon","description":"Amazon","dateCreated":"2022-04-25T19:05:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-06-27T20:43:38+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#pick-n-pay","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"pick-n-pay","dateCreated":"2020-11-09T18:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2021-12-22T20:17:38+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Pick n Pay was founded in South Africa in 1967. Today, it has more than 1,600 stores across southern Africa and employs 40,000 people.In this video, Andrew Mayes, business intelligence specialist at Pick n Pay, explains how rehosting the company’s SAP-based business intelligence platform on Amazon Web Services (AWS) helps it stay relevant and accessible in the digital marketplace.The firm moved from an on-premises infrastructure to one based on Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances. Pick n Pay chose X1 instances, which are designed for running large-scale and in-memory applications like SAP BW/4HANA.Using AWS, Pick n Pay has boosted its agility. It can now replicate its production environment in 2 hours for testing and quickly increase the capacity or performance of instances as needed. Costs have dropped, too, largely because Pick n Pay no longer needs to run a second physical environment for disaster recovery.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Pick-n-Pay_Customer-Reference_Logo@1x.c963ba3d13f95c65661ba2d7df9b5dfa07ca1bad.png","displayLocation":"South Africa","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Retail","sortDate":"2018-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/pick-n-pay-video/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2018","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Pick n Pay Embraces Fresh Thinking on AWS","customer-name":"Pick n Pay"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#location#middle-east-africa","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Middle East \u0026 Africa","description":"Middle East \u0026 Africa","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:30:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:53+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#database-migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Database Migration","description":"Database Migration","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-12T02:01:30+0000"},{"