Content Delivery","description":"Networking \u0026 Content Delivery","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:29+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#iam","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Identity and Access Management","description":"AWS Identity and Access Management","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:03:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:41+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#trusted-advisor","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Trusted Advisor","description":"AWS Trusted Advisor","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:57+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:33:06+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#industry#healthcare-lifesciences","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#industry","name":"healthcare-lifesciences","description":"\u003cp\u003eThis tag is initially being created specifically for the Directory Cards componenet on aws.amazon.com/health/case-studies/. When the GCRP decided to add multilingual content to the CSDIR in 2023, the owners of this page only wanted to display the English content in our Directory. Because the Directory Cards component on their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can use the AND operator to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#pacific-gas-electric-company-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"pacific-gas-electric-company-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:44:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-12T01:40:46+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"PG\u0026E is using the breadth and depth of AWS services to drive its enterprise migration from legacy IT infrastructure to a cloud-first environment. For more than 150 years, PG\u0026E has provided utility services to millions of customers in Northern and Central California.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/case-studies/US/pge-mp-logo.08c1ff470743fe860c876d6dabb06e7b670729c1.png","displayLocation":"Americas","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003ePG\u0026amp;E is using the breadth and depth of AWS services to drive its enterprise migration from legacy IT infrastructure to a cloud-first environment. For more than 150 years, PG\u0026amp;E has provided utility services to millions of customers in Northern and Central California. In addition to using dozens of AWS services including Amazon Aurora, Amazon Kinesis, and Amazon Glacier, PG\u0026amp;E also uses the AWS Partner Network to speed its journey to the cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Power \u0026 Utilities","sortDate":"2017-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/pacific-gas-electric/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Pacific Gas \u0026 Electric Company","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2017","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Pacific Gas \u0026 Electric Company Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#glacier","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon S3 Glacier","description":"Amazon S3 Glacier","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:03:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#video","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Video","description":"Video","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:11+0000"},{"id":