, and Amazon Athena. Siemens PLM provides product-lifecycle management software to thousands of companies and follows an \u0026quot;AWS first\u0026quot; strategy to power its MindSphere industrial IoT platform.\u003c/p\u003e\n","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Siemens_Customer-Reference_Logo%401x.bb038521df5899223d4bd8364182c2fc69ef288d.png","displayLocation":"Germany","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eUsing an \u001cAWS-first\u001d strategy, Siemens PLM is driving the digitalization of its core businesses, including customer-facing solutions that require high availability and scalability. The company is headquartered in Germany, with global divisions in industry, energy, healthcare, and infrastructure, and cities. To power its MindSphere industrial IoT platform, Siemens selected AWS and is using more than 40 services including Amazon Kinesis, Amazon OpenSearch Service, and Amazon Athena.\u003c/p\u003e\n","industry":"Power \u0026 Utilities","sortDate":"2017-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/siemens-plm/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Siemens PLM","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2017","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Siemens PLM Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Kinesis","description":"Amazon Kinesis","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:04:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:45+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise","description":"Enterprise","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:39:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-05T01:27:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Serverless","description":"Serverless","dateCreated":"2021-07-28T18:46:39+0000","dateUpdated":"202