-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"fraud-net-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:47:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-14T23:32:44+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"Fraud.net uses AWS to easily build and train machine-learning models to effectively detect online payment fraud. Fraud.net is a leading fraud prevention platform that helps thousands of online merchants detect and prevent fraud. The organization uses Amazon Machine Learning to provide more than 20 machine-learning models and relies on Amazon DynamoDB and AWS Lambda to run code without provisioning or managing servers.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Fraud.net_Customer-Reference_Logo.9c189c40206df8be6f61a423932afd4f46550ce8.png","displayLocation":"Americas","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eRead the Fraud.net customer case study, powered by the AWS cloud. AWS provides cloud computing services to hundreds of thousands of companies.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Software \u0026 Internet","sortDate":"2016-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/fraud-dot-net/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Fraud.net","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2016","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Fraud.net Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Lambda","description":"AWS Lambda","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:04:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:46+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Redshift","description":"Amazon Redshift","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:56+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdat